    44	
    45	### Row classification (rev 2, frozen before any run; mechanical, from the raw timing.jsonl row)
    46	- Rev 2 (codex review 064331 BLOCKING 1-3): the classifier is CODE, not prose: eval/kaggle/classify_rows.py
    47	  (`classify(row)`; sha256 recorded below at freeze, and every summary prints `classifier_sha256`). Its rules, summarised:
    48	- Row evidence (rev 2, wrapper-only change, not on the agent or verification path): each row now carries `result_error`
    49	  (stock TaskResult.error verbatim, <=4096 chars), `agent_error_text`, and `verified_patch_bytes` (length of the stock
    50	  result.agent_patch = the post-strip patch Container B verified). A row missing any of these is H-ROW (schema guard).
    51	- KNOWN-DIAG (a flag, not an error, never gating): over EVERY `setup.py` entry in `setup_calls` (one per installation pass;
    52	  passes are no longer judged from the overwritten `editable_failed` / `setup_subprocesses` fields), each failing editable
    53	  subprocess is either the offline attempt (`--no-index`) whose output contains `uninstall-no-record-file`, or an online
    54	  fallback (no `--no-index`) that follows such a failure in the same pass. The fallback's own output need not contain the
    55	  diagnostic (rev 1's predicate rejected this documented chain: 0/7 matches on arm F; rev 2 matches 7/7). Same marker
    56	  accepted for a failing `workspace_editable` step. Docs: docs/GOLD_CALIBRATION.md v2; the 48-clean gold/null calibration ran
    57	  in the same docker-path.
    58	- HARNESS (H), precedence H-ROW > H-SETUP > H-VERIFY:
    59	  H-ROW = row missing; schema guard; wrapper `error` naming an evaluation/cleanup/trace-parse/row-build exception; or any
    60	  non-empty `result_error`/`agent_error_text` that is neither a known agent end state (timeout/turns/tool_calls/no_submit)
    61	  nor a stock verification message caused by the agent patch (`Failed to apply agent patch:`, the JUnit/required-node
    62	  family in swegemma verification.py). So `Evaluation error:`, `Failed to apply test_patch:`, `Missing test specification`
    63	  and unrecognised text stay H (fail closed); the wrapper's generic `Harness task failure` is re-derived from the two texts.
    64	  H-SETUP = missing_tool_deps; a fatal step rc != 0; a `setup.py` rc != 0; any failing editable subprocess outside the
    65	  KNOWN-DIAG chain in ANY pass; or setup_failed=True with none of these and no KNOWN-DIAG (unexplained).
    66	  H-VERIFY = verified_patch_bytes > 0, not a patch-apply failure, and exit_code not an int in {0..5, 124}.
    67	  vLLM not up = the whole kernel is void.
    68	- AGENT outcomes (quality, never validity, never rerun): PASS = stock resolved=True; NO_PATCH (verified_patch_bytes 0);
    69	  PATCH_APPLY; VERIFY_TIMEOUT_124 (the patch hangs pytest, review item 2); PYTEST_1; PYTEST_2_5; EXIT0_UNRESOLVED
    70	  (JUnit/required nodes); OTHER_FAIL. `agent_end` (timeout/turns/...) is recorded alongside, descriptive.
